>> title: Mayu
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: japanese, garlic, ramen, aroma oil, black
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: mayu, 麻油, black garlic oil, burnt garlic oil, ma-yu, black oil, the black float on tonkotsu
>> pairs-with: tonkotsu-ramen
>> servings: 12
>> time: 30 min

>> step: A controlled burn: this is supposed to smell scorched, and there are about thirty seconds between right and ruined.
A controlled burn: this is supposed to smell scorched, and there are about thirty seconds between right and ruined.

>> step: fry to black, 12 min
Fry @garlic{1%head}(about 12 cloves, minced fine) in @neutral oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in a small #saucepan{} over medium-low heat ~fry{12%min}, stirring the whole time.

>> step: blitz to a loose black paste
Blitz @&(~1)black garlic{} with @toasted sesame oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #blender{} until it is a loose paste with no grit left in it.

>> step: cool and settle 15 min
Cool @&(~1)mayu{} ~cool{15%min} and let the solids settle.
